# Dependency cooldown (OPE-920, re-scoped OPE-945): NOT set here.
#
# A `min-release-age` cooldown blunts a fresh-publish supply-chain attack: a
# compromised package version has a window to get caught and unpublished
# before a project's `npm install` will touch it. Under OPE-945,
# that trade-off is CONSUMER guidance for projects that build on Open
# Everywhere, not a gate on Open Everywhere's own dependency intake — our
# largest-blast-radius dependency, eve, ships several times a day, so a
# multi-day cooldown would keep this repo permanently behind it. See the
# "Dependency cooldown" section of docs/introduction/quick-start.md for the
# guidance we ship to consumers who want this control in their own project.
